<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    ORDER 20, AND IT MUST NOT DRIFT.

    Verified against the shipped defs in Data/, 2026-08-13:

        Terrain     0      Tiles       5      Lakes     150
        Rivers    200      AncientSites 300   AncientRoads 400
        Pollution 450      Factions   500     Roads     600
        Landmarks 650      Mutators   700     Features 1000

    Nothing vanilla sits between 5 and 150, so 20 has a 145-wide gap to itself.

    ⭐ The order IS the feature. We do not build rivers — we finish before vanilla
    builds them, so vanilla's own river step at 200 flows into the seas this step
    just made. Later than Lakes/Rivers and the rivers, roads, landmarks and
    mutators would all have been chosen against a coastline that no longer exists.

    Earlier than 5 would be worse: Tiles has not assigned biomes or elevation yet,
    so there would be nothing to read and nothing to raise.
  -->
  <WorldGenStepDef>
    <defName>Jawa_SeaShaping</defName>
    <order>20</order>
    <worldGenStep Class="JawaSeaShaper.WorldGenStep_JawaSea" />
  </WorldGenStepDef>

</Defs>
